+# Interpreter source provenance and local adaptation
+
+Source repository: https://github.com/moleworld-dev/touchhle-arm-interpreter
+
+Pinned commit: `adffbbdae912568557f33f8596110cc677809641`.
+
+License: Mozilla Public License 2.0; the upstream `LICENSE` is preserved in this directory and each adapted Rust file retains its MPL header. The upstream project attributes its interpreter implementation to touchHLE. That provenance statement is the upstream author's statement; this integration does not assert that the interpreter is part of the official touchHLE release.
+
+Files adapted: `mod.rs`, `arm.rs`, `thumb16.rs`, `thumb32.rs`, `vfp.rs`.
+
+Integration target: Applesauce commit `c75278bda86c80cbcec2d8d1493b5be9d5a9e0d1`.
+
+## Local changes
+
+- CPU state/error imports now use Applesauce's `crate::cpu` namespace.
+- The decoder uses Applesauce's existing guest memory and pointer types; no second 4 GiB guest memory allocation is created.
+- `CpuContext` gains `Debug` for compatibility with host diagnostics.
+- Guest context switching clears the local exclusive reservation.
+- A zero instruction budget returns before executing a guest instruction.
+- The loaded image's null segment is checked even when the direct-memory option is disabled.
+- Unimplemented Thumb system instructions halt instead of using the upstream broad successful no-op fallback.
+- Unmodeled VFP system register reads/writes halt instead of returning fabricated zero values or ignoring writes.
+- FPSCR-directed VCVTR conversions halt explicitly; truncation is not substituted for rounding.
+- Unhandled A32 miscellaneous instructions (including MRS/MSR/BKPT) cannot fall through to generic TST/TEQ/CMP/CMN semantics.
+- Unmodeled A32 exception returns (result-writing S+PC) and banked/status LDM/STM forms halt before side effects.
+- Debug suspicious-control-flow heuristics are log-only; zero is a valid ARM/Thumb opcode and cannot justify an undefined-instruction trap.
+- CLREX clears the local exclusive monitor; empty ARM LDM/STM register lists halt instead of silently succeeding.
+- VMOV core/single register transfers correctly decode bit7 as the low bit of the S-register index, including odd registers; the scalar-D handler is restricted to its cp11 encoding. This fixes a reached decoder error in libgcc's s15-based float-to-integer conversions, which had returned unchanged float bits and zeroed the game's 16-bit screen dimensions.
+
+The `moleworld_compat`, `interp_debug`, `interp_hb`, and underscore-named differential-harness features are not defined by the host integration, so their upstream optional paths are disabled. No G1-specific instruction bypass, fake result, or undefined-instruction fallback is added.
+
+## Build selection
+
+The normal desktop default remains `static,cpu-dynarmic`. Add `--features cpu-interpreter` for a desktop interpreter run; the interpreter takes precedence if both CPU features are present. To omit Dynarmic compilation entirely, use `--no-default-features --features static,cpu-interpreter`.
+
+The iOS entry crate forwards `cpu-dynarmic` by default to preserve its prior behavior. A no-JIT core can be selected explicitly with `--no-default-features --features cpu-interpreter` when building `platform/ios/rust-entry/Cargo.toml`.
+
+**The iOS host UI also has a separate JIT launch gate. This CPU patch does not change that host gate, produce an IPA, or establish iPhone XR performance.** An iOS no-JIT build needs host capability reporting and a corresponding launch decision, along with normal Apple SDK compilation and device tests.
+
+## Bounded verification before full game integration
+
+Unmodified upstream release tests: four integration tests passed, and one documentation example compiled. The substantial source-embedded differential tests are disabled in that standalone repository because its Dynarmic oracle/features are absent; they must not be counted as executed.
+
+The integration's isolated CPU-contract harness passed fourteen tests: ARM/Thumb SVC PC advancement, branch-with-link mode preservation, integer/VFP/status context preservation, zero-budget behavior, strict null reads, failure on an unimplemented Thumb system-register instruction, failure for A32 miscellaneous/system encodings, explicit failure on FPSCR-directed VCVTR, fail-closed exception returns and banked transfers, valid zero instructions in ARM and Thumb debug execution, exact libgcc s15 float-to-integer sequences, and direct all-32-S-register transfer checks in both instruction states. Both new VMOV regressions failed before the decoder correction and passed afterward. That harness uses the real adapted CPU code and upstream memory storage exposed through Applesauce-compatible inherent methods. It does not substitute for compiling or running the entire Applesauce host.
+
+## Known scope limits
+
+Instruction coverage is not exhaustive. Source review found no A32 LDREX/STREX implementation, while Thumb-2 exclusive operations do exist. Floating-point emulation uses host arithmetic. FPSCR-directed VCVTR conversions now halt explicitly. Arithmetic and precision conversions do not fully implement FPSCR rounding-mode controls; VCMP/VCMPE currently share the same comparison path and do not distinguish signaling-exception behavior. Floating-point cumulative exception bits, enabled exception traps, flush-to-zero/default-NaN controls, and NaN payload/denormal behavior are not comprehensively modeled or verified. VCVT truncating conversions use saturating helper behavior but do not update all architectural status flags. These are correctness limits, not claims of hardware-equivalent VFP emulation. The main game may avoid some of these paths; only reached-instruction evidence and comparison against the known working Dynarmic run can decide which must be implemented next.
+
+This code is a CPU backend integration, not decompiled game source. The original game logic remains the uploaded ARM32 binary interpreted as guest data.
